  - title: The offer
    number: 8
    heartsNeeded: 8
    path: 0
    conditions:
      days: 0
      seasons: 0
      dayFrom: 0
      dayTo: 0
      minYear: 0
      minTotalDays: 0
      weather: 0
      requireFlags: []
      anyFlags: []
      forbidFlags: []
      counters: []
    pages:
    - A woman from the tower stopped me on the round today. Very polite. Very good shoes.
    - '''Logistics supervisor. Sterling Parcel Network.'' A desk, a chair, three times the pay, and no more wet socks. I''d run the lockers. All of them.'
    - Or Lucia says if the whole street signs a petition, city hall has to look at the round again. Every door. Every name.
    - Grace says I should decide with my heart. My heart says my feet hurt. What do you say?
    happy: 0
    ask:
      item: {fileID: 0}
      amount: 0
      minQuality: 0
      questTitle: 
      questText: 
      reminder: []
      thanks: []
    choice:
      enabled: 1
      optionA: Start the petition
      replyA:
      - A petition it is. I'll start with Gus, because if Gus signs, everybody signs, just to disagree with him.
      - And I know every door on this street. That's the one advantage I've got over a yellow box.
      flagsA:
      - mail_petition
      optionB: Take the tower job
      replyB:
      - A desk. Dry socks. Three times the pay. Nia can have football boots that fit.
      - I'll tell the post office tomorrow. Somebody else will do the round. Somebody will.
      flagsB:
      - emeka_tower_job
    setFlags: []
    reward:
      gold: 0
      item: {fileID: 0}
      amount: 0
      friendship: 0
  - title: Every door
    number: 9
    heartsNeeded: 9
    path: 1
    conditions:
      days: 0
      seasons: 0
      dayFrom: 0
      dayTo: 0
      minYear: 0
      minTotalDays: 0
      weather: 0
      requireFlags: []
      anyFlags: []
      forbidFlags: []
      counters: []
    pages:
    - Two hundred and six names! The whole street, the store, Frank's, and half the city hall staff. Kenji signed in calligraphy. It took him an hour.
    - Lucia carried it into the council meeting herself. The lockers are staying, but so am I. Six days a week, like before.
    - 'And look: nobody''s using the lockers. The yellow doors just sit there, shut. People would rather wait for a knock.'
    happy: 1
    ask:
      item: {fileID: 0}
      amount: 0
      minQuality: 0
      questTitle: 
      questText: 
      reminder: []
      thanks: []
